    q("patterns", "medium", ["design-patterns"], "Explain the repository pattern and the observer pattern and give a use for each.", "A repository hides how data is stored behind a simple interface so business code does not depend on the database. The observer pattern lets objects subscribe to changes of another object, such as UI parts updating when data changes.", ["Repository abstracts storage", "Observer: subscribe to changes", "A use for each"], ["How does the repository help testing?"]),
